{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70f83207-964d-47d5-9aaa-952fdf9aaabd","step":{"id":"s1","script":"On a unit circle, an angle selects a point. We will track its height as the angle increases.","ops":[{"op":"sketch","id":"circle","region":"left","strokes":[[[0.85,0.45],[0.823,0.584],[0.747,0.697],[0.634,0.773],[0.5,0.8],[0.366,0.773],[0.253,0.697],[0.177,0.584],[0.15,0.45],[0.177,0.316],[0.253,0.203],[0.366,0.127],[0.5,0.1],[0.634,0.127],[0.747,0.203],[0.823,0.316],[0.85,0.45]],[[0.08,0.45],[0.92,0.45]],[[0.5,0.87],[0.5,0.03]],[[0.5,0.45],[0.747,0.203]]]},{"op":"text","id":"circlelabel","anchor":{"el":"circle","side":"above","gap":0.03},"content":"Unit circle: radius = 1"},{"op":"axes","id":"waveaxes","region":"right","x":{"min":0,"max":6.2832,"label":"\\theta\\text{ (radians)}"},"y":{"min":-1.2,"max":1.2,"label":"y"}}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70f83207-964d-47d5-9aaa-952fdf9aaabd","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Measure the angle counterclockwise from the positive horizontal axis. The selected point has height sine theta.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"coordinates","anchor":{"el":"circle","side":"below","gap":0.03},"latex":"P=(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)"},{"op":"text","id":"height","anchor":{"el":"coordinates","side":"below","gap":0.04},"content":"height = \\sin\\theta"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"70f83207-964d-47d5-9aaa-952fdf9aaabd","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70f83207-964d-47d5-9aaa-952fdf9aaabd","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Plot that height against angle. One counterclockwise revolution traces one complete sine wave.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"sinewave","axes_id":"waveaxes","expr":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.283185307179586]},{"op":"equation","id":"quarterturns","anchor":{"el":"waveaxes","side":"below","gap":0.04},"latex":"(\\theta,\\sin\\theta):\\ (0,0),\\ (\\frac{\\pi}{2},1),\\ (\\pi,0),\\ (\\frac{3\\pi}{2},-1),\\ (2\\pi,0)"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"At the bottom of the unit circle, what angle and sine value do we plot?","expected_gist":"The angle is 3 pi over 2 radians and the sine value is negative one."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70f83207-964d-47d5-9aaa-952fdf9aaabd","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Another revolution repeats the same heights. The sine wave has amplitude one and period two pi.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"amplitude","anchor":{"el":"height","side":"below","gap":0.05},"content":"Radius 1 \\Rightarrow amplitude 1"},{"op":"equation","id":"period","anchor":{"el":"quarterturns","side":"below","gap":0.05},"latex":"\\sin(\\theta+2\\pi)=\\sin\\theta"}],"checkpoint":null}}
